In-in sign algebra:
<Q H_int> - <H_int Q> = z - z* = 2 i Im(z)
-i <[Q,H_int]> = +2 Im(z)
Therefore a displayed -2 Im(I_v) requires I_v=<Q L_int>=-<Q H_int>,
or another explicit extra-minus definition; v1.7.118 defines neither.
